From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Branson <andrew.branson@jolla.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:14:22 +0200
Subject: [sailfishos][build] Enable llama half precision on ARM32

GCC only exposes __fp16 on 32-bit Arm when a half-precision format is
selected. Mirror llama.cpp's CMake configuration in its Gecko
moz.build integration.
---
 third_party/llama.cpp/moz.build | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/llama.cpp/moz.build b/third_party/llama.cpp/moz.build
index 4799456eb625..c71ab026f74b 100644
--- a/third_party/llama.cpp/moz.build
+++ b/third_party/llama.cpp/moz.build
@@ -46,6 +46,12 @@ elif CONFIG['TARGET_CPU'] == 'aarch64':
     SOURCES += files['ARM64_SOURCES']
 elif CONFIG['TARGET_CPU'] == 'arm':
     SOURCES += files['ARM_SOURCES']
+
+    # GCC requires an explicit half-precision format before it exposes
+    # __fp16 on 32-bit Arm. Keep this in sync with llama.cpp's CMake build.
+    if CONFIG['CC_TYPE'] == 'gcc':
+        CFLAGS += ['-mfp16-format=ieee']
+        CXXFLAGS += ['-mfp16-format=ieee']
 else:
     DEFINES["GGML_CPU_GENERIC"] = 1
 
